  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Iran Developing a Gender Sensitive Approach to Monitoring and Evaluation in Development Planning</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot; Help integrate gender sensitive monitoring and evaluation indicators/mechanisms in the preparation and implementation of the Fourth Five-Year-Development-Plan. Certain circumstances changed between the time that the grant was terminated in 2003 and then re-activated in 2006. Thus it became necessary to make certain ammendments in order to ensure effective implementation of the grant and its development objectives.  Accordingly the following ammendments have been made to the annex (TORs) to the letter of Agreement:  1. Item (ii) in the first sub-paragraph of paragraph 1.1 which lists various purposes of the grant is deleted.  2. A new clause (v) is added to Part A (&quot;&quot;Research and Studies&quot;&quot;) of paragraph 1.1 to read as follows:  (v) Research topics that have emerged as priority issues since the adoption of the Fourth Five-Year Development Plan.  3. A new clause (v) is added to Part B (&quot;&quot;Training&quot;&quot;):  (v) Subject to agreement between the Bank and the Recipientcomma the development of a curriculum for a Masters&apos; degree in gender studies.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
